tools help airk_search.stdout:
{"exit":0,"message":"","stdout":"search
Find concepts, code or documents; prose/comments and source can rank together. For a named type/function, prefer symbols first, scoped references for textual uses, then bounded read_file; search supplements that investigation. Scope by literal path_prefix, exact indexed language, metadata-based evidence_kind or exclude_path_prefix; documents alone do not prove application behavior. Omitted mode retains saved hybrid/vector policy; explicit lexical normalizes punctuation and quotes into AND terms; quotes do not enable phrase matching. Lexical candidates use stable-id order, not relevance ranking. Eligible Default search can return lexical evidence during a helper outage; execution records served mode and semantic incompleteness. Explicit vector/hybrid and saved RequireComplete refuse helper outages. Vector/hybrid need the indexed local model. semantic=true aliases vector. Bounded native-definition pointers may accompany identifiers without changing ranking. Focused cited snippets are default; full_chunks requests whole indexed chunks. Read guidance for returned limitations; empty matches alone establish no cause. Check readiness/truncation and use response_mode=full for provenance audits.

Input schema (required arguments and defaults):
{
  "$defs": {
    "EvidenceKind": {
      "enum": [
        "code",
        "document",
        "configuration",
        "unknown"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "ResponseMode": {
      "enum": [
        "terse",
        "full"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "SearchMode": {
      "enum": [
        "lexical",
        "vector",
        "hybrid"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "dependentRequired": {
    "index_ids": [
      "project_ids"
    ],
    "member_availability": [
      "project_ids"
    ]
  },
  "properties": {
    "evidence_kind": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/EvidenceKind"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Indexed evidence category, based on extraction metadata rather than filename suffix."
    },
    "exclude_path_prefix": {
      "description": "Optional literal collection-relative prefix to exclude; does not change source authorization.",
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "full_chunks": {
      "description": "Return complete indexed chunks instead of focused snippets.",
      "type": [
        "boolean",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "include_status": {
      "default": false,
      "description": "Include current freshness/readiness even when unchanged on this connection.",
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "index_ids": {
      "description": "Optional explicit index subset of the selected Projects. Qualified follow-up reads require one originating index.",
      "items": {
        "pattern": "^idx_[0-9a-f]{32}$",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "maxItems": 32,
      "minItems": 1,
      "type": "array",
      "uniqueItems": true
    },
    "language": {
      "description": "Exact indexed extraction-language/profile label, as reported by file_info.",
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "limit": {
      "default": 10,
      "format": "uint",
      "maximum": 100,
      "minimum": 1,
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "max_bytes": {
      "default": 8192,
      "format": "uint",
      "maximum": 65536,
      "minimum": 1,
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "member_availability": {
      "default": "report",
      "description": "Report retains usable data and complete member failures. Require returns non-success if any selected member cannot answer; independent of saved-source verification.",
      "enum": [
        "report",
        "require"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "mode": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SearchMode"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Omit for the saved collection policy; pending vectors are disclosed in the response."
    },
    "origin_publication": {
      "description": "Exact originating member publication token. Requires one selected index; a different member publication expires the follow-up rather than substituting newer evidence.",
      "maxLength": 256,
      "minLength": 1,
      "type": "string"
    },
    "path_prefix": {
      "description": "Optional literal collection-relative path prefix, not a glob.",
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "project_ids": {
      "description": "Explicit Projects within the frozen reviewed connection grant. Omission keeps the connection's captured selection; no workspace or saved-default expansion.",
      "items": {
        "pattern": "^prj_[0-9a-f]{32}$",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "maxItems": 32,
      "minItems": 1,
      "type": "array",
      "uniqueItems": true
    },
    "query": {
      "description": "Default hybrid retrieval; lexical normalizes punctuation/quotes into AND terms, not phrase matching.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "reply_detail": {
      "description": "Lean/Rich changes available fact projection, never retention. Reads without an alternate projection keep their existing payload. Omission preserves legacy defaults; conflicts with compact reject. Search full_chunks is independent.",
      "enum": [
        "lean",
        "rich",
        null
      ],
      "type": [
        "string",
        "null"
      ]
    },
    "response_mode": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ResponseMode"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Terse is default. Use full for provenance/coverage audits, readiness diagnosis or unexpected results; it does not resolve calls or verify live source."
    },
    "semantic": {
      "default": false,
      "description": "Compatibility alias for vector-only retrieval.",
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "verification": {
      "default": "report",
      "description": "Report is the default: bounded dated saved-byte outcomes. Off skips source checks; require fails unless every returned file reference matches. No extraction, completeness or unsaved-buffer certification.",
      "enum": [
        "off",
        "report",
        "require"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
    "verification_deadline_ms": {
      "default": 2000,
      "description": "Cooperative deadline, 1..30000 ms; default 2000. Blocking filesystem calls retain capacity until they return.",
      "maximum": 30000,
      "minimum": 1,
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "verification_max_bytes": {
      "default": 16777216,
      "description": "Aggregate raw-byte budget, 1..1073741824; default 16777216 (16 MiB).",
      "maximum": 1073741824,
      "minimum": 1,
      "type": "integer"
    },
    "verification_max_sources": {
      "default": 8,
      "description": "Maximum whole-source checks, 1..256; default 8.",
      "maximum": 256,
      "minimum": 1,
      "type": "integer"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "query"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}

Argument template (replace placeholders; follow schema constraints):
{
  "include_status": false,
  "limit": 10,
  "max_bytes": 8192,
  "member_availability": "report",
  "query": "<query>",
  "semantic": false,
  "verification": "report",
  "verification_deadline_ms": 2000,
  "verification_max_bytes": 16777216,
  "verification_max_sources": 8
}

Save arguments as query.json, then run with your collection options:
  airkctl tools call airk_search --args-file query.json
Inside the tools console:
  call airk_search --args-file query.json
  call airk_search {"include_status":false,"limit":10,"max_bytes":8192,"member_availability":"report","query":"<query>","semantic":false,"verification":"report","verification_deadline_ms":2000,"verification_max_bytes":16777216,"verification_max_sources":8}

Explicit vector search (requires a published model/index and discloses partial coverage):
  call airk_search {"query":"how is a forgotten password recovered","mode":"vector","limit":5}
Omit mode for the saved collection search policy.
"}
